====== modman. Module manager for frugal / live-CD Linux ======

**Language:** English | [[Home-ru|Русский]]

  * **modman** is a CLI backend for managing squashfs/erofs PFS modules on frugal / live-CD Linux systems that use AUFS or OverlayFS.
  * **modman-gui** is an optional GTK3 frontend.
  * **modman-tui** is an optional dialog-based terminal frontend.
  * **modman-open** is a GTK3 file-manager opener for one local ''.pfs'' file. It supports inspect/load/unload through ''modman'' only; it does not replace the full manager.
  * Runtime filesystem work is delegated to [[https://github.com/sfs-pra/pfs-utils-05/wiki|pfs-utils]] v5: ''pfsload'', ''pfsunload'', ''pfsinfo'', ''pfsbench'' and related tools.
  * Supported boot stacks are detected through pfs-utils: **rootaufs2**, **UIRD**, **Porteus**, and **livekit**.
  * The ''--machine'' TSV contract is stable for GUI, TUI and scripts. Fields are tab-separated and locale-independent.
  * [[https://forum.puppyrus.org/index.php?board=213.0|Discussion]]
  * [[https://github.com/sfs-pra/modman|Download / sources]]

====== Architecture overview ======

modman is a three-tier system:

  - **pfs-utils v5** — runtime layer: AUFS/OverlayFS mount and unmount, format detection, boot-stack detection, module build/extract helpers.
  - **modman** (Bash CLI) — contract layer: machine schema, command routing, validation, dependency handling, calls to ''pfs*'' tools.
  - **modman-gui** (GTK3 C) — optional presentation layer: asynchronous operations, cancellation, debounced search, details panes and polkit integration.
  - **modman-tui** (Bash + dialog) — optional terminal frontend. It calls only ''modman --machine''.

Frontends do not access filesystem layers directly. GUI, TUI and file opener all go through ''modman --machine''.

====== Components ======

^ Package ^ Binary ^ Role ^ Depends on ^
| ''modman'' | ''modman'' | CLI backend and ''--machine'' contract | ''bash'', ''pfs-utils5 >= 2026.04'' |
| ''modman-gui'' | ''modman-gui'', ''modman-open'' | GTK3 manager and file opener | ''modman'', ''gtk3'', ''glib2'', ''polkit'' |
| ''modman-tui'' | ''modman-tui'' | dialog terminal frontend | ''modman'', ''dialog'', ''gettext'' |

====== Core concepts ======

===== Modules and identity =====

  * **Module** — a squashfs or erofs archive containing a filesystem tree rooted at ''/''.
  * **PFS module** — a module built by **mkpfs** or **mkpfs-erofs**. It carries metadata such as ''pfs.files'', ''pfs.specs'' and ''pfs.depends''.
  * **Simple module** — built from one source.
  * **Composite module** — built from several sources and later split/extracted by pfs-utils.
  * **identity** — the short cache key derived from the filename by trimming version, architecture and revision tags.

<code text>
evince-gtk3-p-3.26.0_64-sf06.pfs  ->  evince-gtk3-p
030-gtk3-2601-sf03.pfs            ->  030-gtk3
</code>

===== Module states =====

^ State ^ Source command ^ Meaning ^
| Loaded before | ''modman --list-loaded-before'' / ''-Lb'' | Base modules attached by initrd. Unloading mutates the running base. |
| Loaded after | ''modman --list-loaded-after'' / ''-La'' | Hot-attached at runtime. Safe to unload. |
| Local | ''modman --list-local'' / ''-Ql'' | Downloaded ''.pfs'' files that are not attached. |
| Repo / online | ''modman -Ss <query>'' | Remote search results overlaid with matching local files. |

These states map directly to the GUI tabs: **Подключенные**, **Инет**, **Локальные**, **Система**.

====== Command-line interface ======

All common operations support two dialects:

  * **pacman-style**: ''modman -S'', ''modman -R'', ''modman -Ss'', ''modman -Sy''.
  * **apt-style**: ''modman install'', ''modman remove'', ''modman search'', ''modman update''.

===== Quickstart =====

<code bash>
# Sync the index cache with mirrors
modman -Sy

# Search the repository
modman -Ss evince

# Install: resolve dependencies, download, attach via pfsload
sudo modman -S evince

# List modules attached after boot
modman --list-loaded-after

# Detach a runtime module
sudo modman -R evince

# Remove a downloaded local file
modman -Rl evince
</code>

===== Load-mode and path overrides =====

<code bash>
sudo modman --lower -S evince          # attach to the lower AUFS layer
sudo modman --toram -S evince          # copy into tmpfs before mounting
sudo modman -d /tmp/modman-cache -S evince
sudo modman -S /path/to/module.pfs
</code>

====== The --machine contract ======

''--machine'' switches stdout to tab-separated values, suppresses colored human messages and keeps diagnostics on stderr. It is the only API consumed by GUI and TUI.

Loaded-module listing uses six fields:

<code text>
name<TAB>layer<TAB>path<TAB>version<TAB>mount_mode<TAB>mount_in_ram
</code>

Update check uses eleven fields:

<code text>
update<TAB>id<TAB>name<TAB>old_version<TAB>new_version<TAB>installed_path<TAB>candidate_filename<TAB>repo<TAB>risk<TAB>reboot_required<TAB>message
</code>

The ''risk'' field classifies each update:

  * **normal** — module is not loaded in the current session.
  * **loaded** — module is hot-attached at runtime; update is safe and takes effect after reboot.
  * **system** — module is attached by initrd; applying it requires ''--confirm-system-updates''.

When ''reboot_required=1'', modman appends the literal line ''нужна перезагрузка'' to machine output. Parsers must match it verbatim. Reboot is never performed automatically.

====== GUI, TUI and opener ======

===== modman-gui =====

''modman-gui'' is the full GTK3 manager. It uses asynchronous cancellable backend calls and parses only ''modman --machine'' output.

<code bash>
modman-gui
modman-gui --updates
</code>

===== modman-open =====

''modman-open'' is for file-manager "Open with..." flows. Supported MIME type: ''application/x-pfs''. Desktop integration uses ''modman-open.desktop'' with ''Exec=modman-open %f''.

Supported scope: show one local ''.pfs'', load it through ''modman -S <path>'' and unload it through ''modman -R <name>''. It does not support catalog search, updates, tabs, package extraction or batch open.

===== modman-tui =====

''modman-tui'' is a terminal frontend built on ''dialog''.

<code bash>
modman-tui
</code>

Environment variables for tests and runtime overrides: ''MODMAN_BIN'', ''DIALOG_BIN'', ''MODMAN_TUI_TMPDIR''.

====== Update management ======

<code bash>
modman -Sy
modman --machine --check-updates
sudo modman --update <id>
sudo modman --update-all
sudo modman --update-all --confirm-system-updates
modman --update-blacklist-add evince-3.26.0.pfs
modman --machine --check-updates --include-blacklisted
</code>

''modman-update-check'' is an XDG autostart helper. It runs ''modman --machine --check-updates'' at login and sends a ''notify-send'' notification only. It never applies updates.

====== Configuration ======

Configuration is read in increasing priority:

  - ''/usr/share/modman/modman.conf'' — shipped defaults.
  - ''/etc/modman.conf'' — system-wide configuration.
  - ''~/.config/modman/modman.conf'' or ''$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/modman/modman.conf'' — per-user override.

Key variables:

^ Variable ^ Purpose ^
| ''DOWNLOAD_DIR'' | Where modules are downloaded. Auto-detected on rootaufs2 when possible. |
| ''AUFS_INITRD_PREFIX'' | Prefix used to classify initrd/base modules. |
| ''EXT'' | Module extension, default ''pfs''. |
| ''CLI_STYLE'' | ''pacman'' or ''apt''. |
| ''CMD_LOAD'' / ''CMD_UNLOAD'' | Runtime load/unload commands. Defaults: ''pfsload'' / ''pfsunload''. |
| ''REPO_URLS'' | Repository mirror list. |
| ''MODMAN_STATE_DIR'' | Persistent state directory, default ''/var/lib/modman''. |
| ''UPDATE_CHECK_ON_LOGIN'' | ''1'' or ''0'' for login-time update checking. |

See ''modman.conf(5)'' for the full reference.

====== Boot stacks and AUFS / OverlayFS behavior ======

modman delegates boot-stack and layering detection to pfs-utils plugin detectors:

^ Detector ^ initrd ^ Layering ^ AUFS prefix ^
| ''10-uird.sh'' | uird | overlay | ''${SYSMNT}/bundles'' |
| ''20-rootaufs2.sh'' | rootaufs2 | aufs | ''/run/archroot/live/memory/images'' |
| ''30-porteus.sh'' | porteus | aufs | ''${SYSMNT}/bundles'' |
| ''40-livekit.sh'' | livekit | overlay | ''${SYSMNT}/bundles'' |

AUFS can append a layer to a live root, so ''pfsload'' / ''pfsunload'' can hot-attach modules system-wide. OverlayFS cannot add a ''lowerdir'' to an active mount. On overlay-root systems, system-wide hot-load is unavailable; use ''pfsrun'' for private namespace execution instead.

Full survey: [[https://github.com/sfs-pra/pfs-utils-05/wiki/aufs-alternatives|AUFS alternatives in the pfs-utils wiki]] ([[https://github.com/sfs-pra/pfs-utils-05/wiki/aufs-alternatives-ru|Русский]]).

====== Installation ======

<code bash>
# Release build from the working tree
makepkg -si

# Build straight from git
makepkg -p PKGBUILD.git -si
</code>

This produces and installs ''modman'', ''modman-gui'' and ''modman-tui'' packages.

====== Dependencies ======

  * //bash//
  * //pfs-utils5 >= 2026.04// (''pfsload'', ''pfsunload'', ''pfsinfo'', ''pfs'', ''pfsbench'')
  * //gtk3//, //glib2// (GUI only)
  * //polkit// (root operations from GUI)
  * //dialog// (TUI only)
  * //gettext// (TUI and localization)
  * //wget// (module and cache downloads)
  * //squashfs-tools// (''.pfs'' handling)
  * //erofs-utils// (optional, erofs modules)
  * //libnotify// (''notify-send'' for login update check)

====== Short aliases ======

^ Long form ^ Alias ^ Mnemonic ^
| ''--list-loaded'' | ''-L'' | List loaded |
| ''--list-loaded-before'' | ''-Lb'' | List loaded before initrd/user split |
| ''--list-loaded-after'' | ''-La'' | List loaded after boot |
| ''--list-local'' | ''-Ql'' | Query local |
| ''--remove-local'' | ''-Rl'' | Remove local |

====== Global flags ======

^ Flag ^ Description ^
| ''--machine'' | TSV output for parsers. |
| ''--confirm-system-updates'' | Allow updating system/base modules. |
| ''--verbose-skips'' | Emit ''skipped'' lines. |
| ''--include-blacklisted'' | Include blacklisted versions in ''--check-updates''. |
| ''-d DIR'' / ''--download-dir DIR'' | Override ''DOWNLOAD_DIR''. |
| ''--progress-file PATH'' | Progress file used by GUI. |
| ''--lower'' | Attach to lower AUFS layer. |
| ''--upper'' | Attach to upper AUFS layer. |
| ''--toram'' | Copy to tmpfs before mounting. |
| ''--load-cmd CMD'' | Override load command. |

